    "q-275237": {
      "dom_id": "step-q275237",
      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "Let $a=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]$ and $b=[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ 3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$ Given that the projection of $a$ onto $b$ is the zero vector, find the value of $x.$\n\n$x=$\n{{field-1}}",
      "worked_solution": "Since $a$ is a nonzero vector, its projection onto another nonzero vector $b$ equals the zero vector only when the vectors are perpendicular. \n\nSo, we must have\n\n$$\na⊥b\\,⟹\\,a\\cdot b=0.\n$$\n\nComputing the dot product, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot b & ={a}_{x}\\cdot {b}_{x}+{a}_{y}\\cdot {b}_{y}+{a}_{z}\\cdot {b}_{z} \\\\  & =-2\\cdot x+1\\cdot 3+2\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =-2x+5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSetting the dot product equal to $0,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot b & =0 \\\\ -2x+5 & =0 \\\\ 2x & =5 \\\\ x & =\\frac{5}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
