    "q-317661": {
      "dom_id": "step-q317661",
      "name": "Question 4",
      "problem": "Let $c=⟨3,-1,2⟩$ and $d=⟨1,1,-1⟩.$ Find the vector projection of $c$ onto $d.$\n\n${\\text{proj}}_{d}\\,c=⟨$\n{{field-1}}$,$\n{{field-2}}$,$\n{{field-3}}\n$⟩$",
      "worked_solution": "Using the formula for the vector projection, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{d}\\,c & =\\frac{c\\cdot d}{d\\cdot d}d \\\\  & =\\frac{{c}_{x}{d}_{x}+{c}_{y}{d}_{y}+{c}_{z}{d}_{z}}{{d}_{x}^{2}+{d}_{y}^{2}+{d}_{z}^{2}}d \\\\  & =\\frac{3\\cdot 1+(-1)\\cdot 1+2\\cdot (-1)}{{1}^{2}+{1}^{2}+(-1)^{2}}d \\\\  & =\\frac{0}{3}d \\\\  & =⟨\\,0,0,0\\,⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
